exports[`spine tone × edge type voice matrix > tone=astronomy: spine prose reads in tone voice 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "Instruments at Custos Echo-58 Belt VI record the dispute between the derelict fleet cluster and Tau Reticuli Cohort as a rising baseline of scarcity: the freight surcharge that lands on them no matter who wins. Reduced to observables, the driver is this — the safety margins were drawn before Derelict fleet cluster started moving. Longshore crews demand danger pay in scrip that clears the same day. The boundary condition nobody can renegotiate: every mitigation contract written against Refugee ark parking orbit has lapsed or failed. Three bodies define this problem: the refugee ark parking orbit, Custos Echo-58 Belt VI, and Custos Echo-58 Belt IV, which absorbs the perturbations. The archived record carries an anomaly both sides decline to discuss: every survey pass returns numbers that contradict the pass before it. Every model of the dispute shares one input: evacuation drills have gone from annual to weekly without an announcement. The derelict fleet cluster versus Custos Echo-58 Belt IV is the headline; the secular decline in conditions at Custos Echo-58 Belt IV Charter is the data. One term in the system does not close: corporate records were altered. Seismic and thermal baselines for Custos Echo-58 Belt IV are extrapolated from Custos Echo-58 Belt IV Charter's single-point coverage.",
  "spineEdgeType": "DESTABILIZES",
  "spineSummary": "Derelict fleet cluster took shape in the third pulse cycle, the perturbation from the derelict fleet cluster now exceeds Tau Reticuli Cohort's tolerance margin.",
}
`;

exports[`spine tone × edge type voice matrix > tone=balanced: spine prose reads in tone voice 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "Granite Reach Water Concession wants control of the schedule everyone else plans around; Kestrel-Locke Salvage Concern guards the records that prove they were here first; Iron Compact Freight Guild gets rationed air while the principals negotiate. For now it stays procedural — filings, audits, and schedules that shave each other thinner. Underneath it runs a complication nobody prices openly: Granite Reach Water Concession broke faith with Kestrel-Locke Salvage Concern in the bleed years. Somebody keeps updating the evacuation postings, and somebody keeps taking them down. Strip away the filings and the cause is plain — the safety margins were drawn before Derelict fleet cluster started moving. Neither the derelict fleet cluster nor Danfeng's Flare Belt III will blink first, and Danfeng's Flare Belt III Cylinder absorbs the difference — family on both sides of the picket line. Evacuation lighters hold at ready-station through every work shift. The principals are the first-wave ghost colony and Danfeng's Flare Belt III; the casualty ledger, so far, is kept at Danfeng's Flare Belt III Cylinder. And there is the part no one says at the negotiating table: the quarantine is political. Prices quoted to the first-wave ghost colony and Danfeng's Flare Belt III differ by a margin every vendor denies. Danfeng's Flare Belt III carries Danfeng's Flare Belt III Cylinder on its surface.",
  "spineEdgeType": "CONTESTS",
  "spineSummary": "The compact between Granite Reach Water Concession and Kestrel-Locke Salvage Concern broke in the bleed years, Everything else in this system is priced against the quarrel between the two of them.",
}
`;

exports[`spine tone × edge type voice matrix > tone=cinematic: spine prose reads in tone voice 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "Brothers of Choir came for standing to rewrite the charter in their own hand; what Long Knife Choir has left to lose is the only leverage they have left to trade. Ask anyone in a dock bar what feeds it and they will tell you straight — every neutral broker who touched this dispute has since recused or vanished. The joint maintenance schedule still runs, but each side sends its own inspector to watch the other's. Nobody pretends anymore; the boundary lines get repainted in daylight. Crown of Dust Pact built something worth taking, and Carrion Synod does the taking in this system. The public channel carries two incompatible traffic advisories for the same lane. Freight insurance for the contested run now costs more than the freight. When the resonance-pumped exocomet swarm and Calvera-10 V finally close, it will be Calvera-10 V Platform standing between them, holding the freight surcharge that lands on them no matter who wins. It is loud now — escort guns, night transfers, and funerals with honor guards. At night the lights of Calvera-10 V Platform are the only argument that Calvera-10 V belongs to anyone.",
  "spineEdgeType": "CONTESTS",
  "spineSummary": "The compact between Brothers of Choir and Long Knife Choir broke in the silent decade, the two of them are bleeding each other dry, and the system cheers them on.",
}
`;
